	=09
	<div class=3D"smittenkitchen-print-hide">
		<p>This is clearly not a pasta bake, but it was supposed to be one. From =
November to December, I was pursued by a vision of an oozy, decadent french=
 onion pasta bake =E2=80=94 that is, the flavors of french onion soup appli=
ed to baked pasta with a bronzed and broiled gruyere topping. What was not =
to love? How could it not be delicious? But it was never right. I made it a=
 few times and I never wanted to eat it. It was too rich and didn=E2=80=99t=
 have enough to bite into, even by the intended standard of holiday indulge=
nce. In the last round, I added cauliflower to it so it felt like more of a=
 pasta-and-vegetable bake and I liked it even less (damp? somehow).</p>
<p><span id=3D"more-66420"></span><br>
<img data-recalc-dims=3D"1" decoding=3D"async" class=3D"alignnone size-larg=
e wp-image-66423" src=3D"https://i0.wp.com/smittenkitchen.com/wp-content/up=
loads/2024/01/french-onion-baked-lentils-and-farro-group.jpg?resize=3D640%2=
C428&amp;quality=3D89&amp;ssl=3D1" alt=3D"" width=3D"640" height=3D"428"></=
p><div class=3D"code-block code-block-3" style=3D"margin: 8px 0; clear: bot=
h;">
<div class=3D"htlad-infeed_medrec_flex"></div>=09
</div>

<p>Then, as if a better idea fairy had been summoned from thin air, or perh=
aps a direct message on Instagram, an Elizabeth from Oakland, CA reached ou=
t and told me she=E2=80=99d made a farro and lentil bake with tons of caram=
elized onions for dinner the night before, told her kids it was french onio=
n soup rice, and they devoured it. =E2=80=9CLiterally just oil (or butter),=
 good stock, wine, onions, farro, lentils and thyme, and gruyere broiled on=
 top,=E2=80=9D she explained. Suddenly it was as if the sun had appeared fr=
om behind the clouds after a week of rain, or removing an entire block of l=
ines in Tetris with a satisfying bloop sound, it was clearly, and retroacti=
vely obviously what I=E2=80=99d have preferred the whole time. I immediatel=
y made it too.</p>
<p><img data-recalc-dims=3D"1" decoding=3D"async" src=3D"https://i0.wp.com/=
live.staticflickr.com/65535/53458362997_9a21b0a749_z.jpg?resize=3D640%2C427=
&amp;quality=3D89&amp;ssl=3D1" alt=3D"french onion baked lentils and farro-=
7" width=3D"640" height=3D"427"></p>
<p>The melodrama ends here, phew, because I think this is perfect; it=E2=80=
=99s loose enough to suggest risotto, hearty enough to be utterly filling, =
and tastes so precisely like french onion soup that I=E2=80=99ll never get =
tired of it. Even cold, days later, I couldn=E2=80=99t stop eating the left=
overs. I thought I=E2=80=99d run it for a final recipe of the year here, a =
luxurious late holiday season dinner, but I believe I took a nap instead. T=
hat brings us to today: It=E2=80=99s cold, rain and wind are heading in our=
 direction, the sun is still setting before 5pm and it=E2=80=99s still dark=
 when we wake, and thus I still be requiring bubbling, cozy dishes with <a =
href=3D"https://twitter.com/AyushiBalani/status/1554429128815783938">cheese=
 on top</a> until things improve. Come join me.</p>
<p><img data-recalc-dims=3D"1" loading=3D"lazy" decoding=3D"async" src=3D"h=
ttps://i0.wp.com/live.staticflickr.com/65535/53459417233_269418119b_z.jpg?r=
esize=3D640%2C427&amp;quality=3D89&amp;ssl=3D1" alt=3D"french onion baked l=
entils and farro-5" width=3D"640" height=3D"427"></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
