			</div><!-- .vcard -->

			<div class=3D"comment-content">
				<p>I know this is an old comment so who knows if you will see this, but=
 I wanted to chime in since this confused me for a long time too. Fluid oun=
ces and ounces as a measurement of weight are not interchangeable, unless y=
ou are measuring water! So a cup of water =3D 8 fluid ounces =3D 8 ounces w=
eight. But, a cup of shredded cheese would not be 8 ounces weight even thou=
gh it takes up 8 fluid ounces of volume. Fluid ounces are volume, ounces ar=
e weight. It=E2=80=99s another case of historical measurements being brough=
t forward in confusing ways.</p>
<p>(And if you really get into it, things are even more complicated, with U=
K and US ounces differing. It can really make your head spin!)</p>
			</div>

