				<b class=3D"fn author-name">
											Annie									</b>
			</div><!-- .vcard -->

			<div class=3D"comment-content">
				<p>This recipe came out perfectly and was delicious! Four adults gobble=
d it up and there were still a couple servings left to put in the fridge fo=
r later. I did make some adjustments:</p>
<p>For GF, I used the same proportion of Lundberg=E2=80=99s Wild Blend rice=
 (mix of brown and wild rices). Also had some homemade chicken stock in the=
 freezer, so used that instead of vegetable broth. Finally, was all out of =
gruyere (!) so substituted Jarlsberg, which is a close cousin; next time I=
=E2=80=99ll use the gruyere as I do love it. </p>
<p>For the lentils, I stuck with French/green/le puy; they hold their shape=
 well=E2=80=94getting soft without becoming mushy=E2=80=94and they don=E2=
=80=99t taste so =E2=80=9Cmuddy=E2=80=9D as brown lentils.</p>
<p>Finally, after cooking in the oven for 50 minutes, it was still too wate=
ry, so I put it back in for another 10-15 minutes, which was perfect for th=
at risotto-like texture.</p>
			</div>

