			</div><!-- .vcard -->

			<div class=3D"comment-content">
				<p>This was delicious =E2=80=94 would be perfect for a casual vegetaria=
n dinner. Crusty bread is non negotiable. I weighed my onions and it took 3=
 large ones. Used Better than Bouillon no- beef for 4 cups of the broth and=
 water for the remaining 2 cups. That plus the 2 tsp kosher salt made it pl=
enty seasoned without being too salty. If you are at high altitude, or if y=
our farro isn=E2=80=99t terribly fresh, you will want to allow longer for t=
he baking phase. It took mine 80 minutes to be tender enough to go to the b=
roiling stage. My grocery store didn=E2=80=99t have Gruy=C3=A8re so I used =
a blend of fontina,  Emmentaler, and Edam. I used closer to 3 cups and that=
 was overkill. It is VERY rich and VERY filling=E2=80=A6 perfect for a cold=
 winter day. If you=E2=80=99re making for 2 people, consider halving the re=
cipe =E2=80=93 it makes a lot and did I mention it is very very rich and fi=
lling. Will definitely make again. Thanks, Deb!</p>
