ter Than Bouillon (chicken), so maybe that was too salty?  If I was going t=
o make it again, I would probably use a tiny bit of salt with the onions an=
d then nothing else.  I used 10 min farro, so I added it after the rest had=
 been in the oven for ~20 min (so it ended up cooking ~25 min). It was cook=
ed well, but still had some bite to it, so it probably would have been fine=
 if I had put it in at the same time as the lentils.  This dish took almost=
 2.5 hours from start to finish (including slicing the onions), and I was d=
isappointed that my family barely ate it.  I am tempted to try to make it a=
gain but I=E2=80=99m not sure I want to spend the time.</p>
